Lawyer Matching Microservice
============================

This repository now contains a FastAPI-based microservice (`lawyer_match_service`) that scores and returns the top-K lawyers for any incoming case payload. Your existing Express backend can call this service over HTTP without needing to embed ML logic directly in Node.js.

Project layout
--------------

```
lawyer_match_service/
  app/
    api.py            # FastAPI routes + dependency wiring
    matching.py       # Embedding-based ranking logic
    models.py         # Pydantic schemas shared across layers
    repository.py     # File/HTTP data sources for lawyer profiles
    encoder.py        # SentenceTransformer wrapper
    config.py         # pydantic-settings configuration
    main.py           # uvicorn entrypoint (app.main:app)
  data/
    lawyers_sample.json
  tests/
    test_matching.py
  requirements.txt
```

Getting started
---------------

```
cd lawyer_match_service
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8010
```

Key environment variables (prefixed with `LAWYER_MATCH_`):

| Variable | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `EMBEDDING_MODEL_NAME` | `sentence-transformers/paraphrase-multilingual-mpnet-base-v2` | HuggingFace model for Thai/English text. |
| `LAWYER_REPOSITORY_PATH` | `./data/lawyers_sample.json` | JSON seed used when no HTTP source is provided. |
| `LAWYER_REPOSITORY_URL` | `None` | Optional Express endpoint returning `{ success, data: [...] }`. |
| `DEFAULT_TOP_K` | `5` | Number of lawyers returned when the client omits `top_k`. |
| `MIN_SCORE_THRESHOLD` | `0.35` | Filters out weak matches. |

API contract
------------

- `POST /match-lawyers`

Request:

```json
{
  "case": {
    "case_id": "2ed9...",
    "title": "โดนข่มขู่คำร้ายร่างกาย",
    "description": "รายละเอียดทั้งหมด...",
    "category": "CRIMINAL",
    "service": "CRIMINAL_DEFENSE",
    "note": "ข้อความเสริม"
  },
  "top_k": 3
}
```

Response:

```json
{
  "case_id": "2ed9...",
  "generated_at": "2025-11-28T05:22:10.210Z",
  "lawyers": [
    {
      "lawyer": { "...entire LawyerProfile..." },
      "score": 0.87,
      "breakdown": {
        "similarity": 0.77,
        "specialization_bonus": 0.1,
        "service_bonus": 0.0
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

- `POST /refresh-lawyers` — forces the service to refetch lawyers (useful after new profiles are added).
- `GET /health` — lightweight readiness probe.

Express integration
-------------------

```ts
import axios from 'axios'

const MATCH_SERVICE_URL = process.env.MATCH_SERVICE_URL ?? 'http://localhost:8010'

export async function getLawyerCandidates(casePayload, topK = 3) {
  const response = await axios.post(`${MATCH_SERVICE_URL}/match-lawyers`, {
    case: casePayload,
    top_k: topK,
  })
  return response.data.lawyers
}
```

Call the helper right after you persist or retrieve a case object; pass the same shape you already expose in Prisma/Mongoose. Add retry logic/timeouts on the Express side according to your deployment requirements.
